## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of practical queue augmentations and min-tracking with guaranteed O(1) per operation.

## Key Concepts
- Min-tracking with stack-based queues
- Amortized analysis of transfers between stacks
- Edge-case handling for empty states and duplicates

## Code Example
```javascript
class MinQueue {
  constructor(){ this.inbox = []; this.outbox = [] }
  _push(stack, val){ const m = stack.length ? Math.min(val, stack[stack.length - 1].min) : val; stack.push({ val, min: m }) }
  enqueue(x){ this._push(this.inbox, x) }
  dequeue(){ if (!this.outbox.length){ while (this.inbox.length){ const el = this.inbox.pop(); const m = this.outbox.length ? Math.min(el.val, this.outbox[this.outbox.length - 1].min) : el.val; this.outbox.push({ val: el.val, min: m }) } }
    return this.outbox.pop().val }
  getMin(){ const mins = []; if (this.inbox.length) mins.push(this.inbox[this.inbox.length - 1].min); if (this.outbox.length) mins.push(this.outbox[this.outbox.length - 1].min); return mins.length ? Math.min(...mins) : undefined }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical understanding of O(1) cache operations using standard data structures and eviction strategy. Emphasizes correct handling of updates, hits, and edge cases (capacity=1, missing keys).

## Key Concepts
- Hash map for O(1) lookups
- Doubly linked list for move-to-front in O(1)
- Eviction of least recently used on overflow
- Edge cases and empty states

## Code Example
```javascript
class LRUCache {
  constructor(capacity) {
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.map = new Map(); // key -> node
    this.head = null;
    this.tail = null;
  }
  _detach(node) {
    if (node.prev) node.prev.next = node.next; else this.head = node.next;
    if (node.next) node.next.prev = node.prev; else this.tail = node.prev;
  }
  _attachAtHead(node) {
    node.prev = null;
    node.next = this.head;
    if (this.head) this.head.prev = node;
    this.head = node;
    if (!this.tail) this.tail = node;
  }
  get(key) {
    const node = this.map.get(key);
    if (!node) return -1;
    this._detach(node);
    this._attachAtHead(node);
    return node.value;
  }
  put(key, value) {
    if (this.map.has(key)) {
      const node = this.map.get(key);
      node.value = value;
      this._detach(node);
      this._attachAtHead(node);
    } else {
      const node = { key, value, prev: null, next: null };
      this.map.set(key, node);
      this._attachAtHead(node);
      if (this.map.size > this.capacity) {
        // evict tail
        const oldTail = this.tail;
        this._detach(oldTail);
        this.map.delete(oldTail.key);
      }
    }
  }
}
```

